From 9d04e524fed2a8e286c06376131abb1f51f92a4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 08:37:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] PortMaster port: Stage3D uploads without a submit,
 consecutive draws in one render pass

RUFFLE_S3D_DEFER_UPLOAD (default on, 0 = old path): a GPU-side Texture.uploadFromBitmapData
no longer submits the renderer's pending work and then the Stage3D encoder (two queue submits,
each a full GL replay plus glFlush on GLES). Both are finished into command buffers and queued
in Descriptors::deferred_command_buffers; every queue submit (renderer or Stage3D) takes the
queue first, so the copy still runs after the offscreen draws it reads and before anything
recorded later.

RUFFLE_S3D_MERGE_PASSES (default on, 0 = old path): drawTriangles joins a pending render pass
on the current target instead of opening its own; the pass is recorded on a target change,
clear, present, or an upload into a buffer or texture it uses. Program constants are kept on
the CPU and copied per draw into a 1 MB uniform ring bound with dynamic offsets, one copy per
pass. Hub on PC: about 30 passes per frame -> about 4.

PM_GPUSTAT=1 also logs submits, queued buffers, presents, Stage3D passes, draws and early pass
ends every 2 s (target pmgpu).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
